{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "episode_id": "cm-flagship-representation-to-evidence-v1",
  "provider": "local_windows_sapi",
  "voice": "Microsoft Mark",
  "dialect": "en-US",
  "rate": 1,
  "volume": 92,
  "sample_rate": 24000,
  "channels": 1,
  "pronunciations": {
    "CM-IR": "C M I R",
    "CSE-flat": "C S E flat",
    "CSE": "C S E",
    "B2": "B two",
    "B4": "B four",
    "EPFL": "E P F L"
  },
  "cues": [
    {
      "cue_id": "ch01-three-questions-01-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch01-three-questions",
      "scene_id": "grid-is-not-headline",
      "text": "A correspondence matrix may look like a grid of zeros and ones, but that picture joins several different questions.",
      "text_sha256": "e74b9cf2cdd77b5178be1bea350dfa6171fb3a18dcd7e164362a6ca129afec96",
      "word_count": 19,
      "planned_start_s": 0.6,
      "planned_end_s": 8.15
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch01-three-questions-01-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch01-three-questions",
      "scene_id": "grid-is-not-headline",
      "text": "We must separate what is represented, how it is computed, and which part a benchmark actually timed.",
      "text_sha256": "8586b2e6ef20d371e483dff210dd095ea4c6d2effe31afd5d264855062b5e957",
      "word_count": 17,
      "planned_start_s": 8.85,
      "planned_end_s": 16.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch01-three-questions-02-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch01-three-questions",
      "scene_id": "separation-map",
      "text": "When those layers are blended, a scoped measurement can quietly become a universal speed claim.",
      "text_sha256": "da63424d53627b8af575ab07187a7ad161e1b19f54167dc0ea1b11e77a0df38f",
      "word_count": 15,
      "planned_start_s": 17.6,
      "planned_end_s": 25.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch01-three-questions-02-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch01-three-questions",
      "scene_id": "separation-map",
      "text": "This episode keeps representation, transformation, preparation, evaluation, and wrapper cost visibly separate from beginning to end.",
      "text_sha256": "fb26182b03763e4cc0b005eaf49d68ba1768a345e35c04deb7d93c58a06aadd4",
      "word_count": 16,
      "planned_start_s": 26.35,
      "planned_end_s": 34.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch01-three-questions-03-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch01-three-questions",
      "scene_id": "episode-roadmap",
      "text": "We will build the explicit matrix, compare it with CM-IR and sharing-aware CSE-flat, then read the corrected evidence.",
      "text_sha256": "0e4310c51a8775a022c2da963e1b79ced0e463b6a0a32fdf25a8f38e9f03687a",
      "word_count": 18,
      "planned_start_s": 35.6,
      "planned_end_s": 43.15
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch01-three-questions-03-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch01-three-questions",
      "scene_id": "episode-roadmap",
      "text": "The goal is not to crown a winner; it is to learn how to ask a precise, reproducible question.",
      "text_sha256": "ee8d830bc0f8f307c97e0404c386f3a046ed47e3f43813210841581bf67a816b",
      "word_count": 19,
      "planned_start_s": 43.85,
      "planned_end_s": 51.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch02-explicit-layout-01-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch02-explicit-layout",
      "scene_id": "expression-to-matrix",
      "text": "Start with the Boolean function x zero exclusive-or x one, inside an ambient universe containing four declared variables.",
      "text_sha256": "8ff9ac63b6f76a35b0c04a958ce8f26356b975d7281ca2dd4e8a99e309a25713",
      "word_count": 18,
      "planned_start_s": 0.6,
      "planned_end_s": 9.15
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch02-explicit-layout-01-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch02-explicit-layout",
      "scene_id": "expression-to-matrix",
      "text": "Only x zero and x one affect the output; x two and x three still determine where repeated values appear in the displayed layout.",
      "text_sha256": "039fae658181da022f339366e94f10df06b4cc19e57b3808a7ed4e2c0c10d12b",
      "word_count": 24,
      "planned_start_s": 9.85,
      "planned_end_s": 18.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch02-explicit-layout-02-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch02-explicit-layout",
      "scene_id": "support-versus-universe",
      "text": "Live support tells us which inputs can change the function, while ambient width tells us how assignments are organized.",
      "text_sha256": "bd198a91c4b2267bd53415520ea6794c39511977797cfda14778e01a5906970c",
      "word_count": 19,
      "planned_start_s": 19.6,
      "planned_end_s": 28.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch02-explicit-layout-02-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch02-explicit-layout",
      "scene_id": "support-versus-universe",
      "text": "Those are both real properties, but they should not be collapsed into one number or used as an automatic engine selector.",
      "text_sha256": "34195eadffe9b738f455129dce20abc10dbe682a4e7fa107fb2b596ad9ac8261",
      "word_count": 21,
      "planned_start_s": 29.35,
      "planned_end_s": 38.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch02-explicit-layout-03-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch02-explicit-layout",
      "scene_id": "matrix-contract",
      "text": "The explicit correspondence matrix is an exact row-and-column truth layout over the declared variable split.",
      "text_sha256": "840f72202a16c116d87a84fcf5c392ea7ad48389b32bfccaab75f54d896ad052",
      "word_count": 15,
      "planned_start_s": 39.6,
      "planned_end_s": 48.15
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch02-explicit-layout-03-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch02-explicit-layout",
      "scene_id": "matrix-contract",
      "text": "That exactness does not imply that materializing the dense layout is always the cheapest way to evaluate or store the same function.",
      "text_sha256": "9f097208bef75543e71636d9596e846d92e3edca87778825c8f29686908b72c5",
      "word_count": 22,
      "planned_start_s": 48.85,
      "planned_end_s": 57.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch03-explicit-versus-ir-01-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch03-explicit-versus-ir",
      "scene_id": "two-artifacts",
      "text": "An explicit CM and CM-IR can describe the same Boolean computation while preserving different information.",
      "text_sha256": "1fbbdf1d1a7db5968b0638763bdc0561382df538b4d70176e84809d7612e8a32",
      "word_count": 15,
      "planned_start_s": 0.6,
      "planned_end_s": 9.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch03-explicit-versus-ir-01-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch03-explicit-versus-ir",
      "scene_id": "two-artifacts",
      "text": "The matrix makes every truth position visible; CM-IR makes canonical nodes, roots, sharing, and reusable compiled structure visible.",
      "text_sha256": "5f54014139f2c1b30fb97f98e4533f3198294b470e709e4a18996c2d31c77d2c",
      "word_count": 18,
      "planned_start_s": 10.35,
      "planned_end_s": 19.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch03-explicit-versus-ir-02-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch03-explicit-versus-ir",
      "scene_id": "ir-evaluation-path",
      "text": "CM-IR can be compiled, interned, persisted, and evaluated without first rebuilding a dense matrix.",
      "text_sha256": "9824821474947e93dd5523aa119e027948e365078b1a48550b9db8e24fb2d12a",
      "word_count": 14,
      "planned_start_s": 20.6,
      "planned_end_s": 29.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch03-explicit-versus-ir-02-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch03-explicit-versus-ir",
      "scene_id": "ir-evaluation-path",
      "text": "A dense CM may still be the required output, but that materialization belongs to a specific output boundary rather than every execution path.",
      "text_sha256": "77928bd28958bb5e8cd2c6b8e0bb65a4d5d67d3e303b70525eebfd9b2a2b7dc1",
      "word_count": 23,
      "planned_start_s": 30.35,
      "planned_end_s": 39.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch03-explicit-versus-ir-03-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch03-explicit-versus-ir",
      "scene_id": "artifact-choice",
      "text": "Use the explicit matrix when the row-and-column truth artifact itself is required, and CM-IR when reusable structure is the question.",
      "text_sha256": "e22eadf924e526a39b26ad2090c665ef8ead2b9ed89f682d1e2cbde97887b7b1",
      "word_count": 20,
      "planned_start_s": 40.6,
      "planned_end_s": 49.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch03-explicit-versus-ir-03-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch03-explicit-versus-ir",
      "scene_id": "artifact-choice",
      "text": "If performance matters, time construction, evaluation, extraction, and repeated reuse separately instead of hiding them behind one method name.",
      "text_sha256": "d1d8afb751e61f0907a49d418b526537da69fb4b8309c9159c010398de17ff05",
      "word_count": 19,
      "planned_start_s": 50.35,
      "planned_end_s": 59.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch04-transformation-mechanisms-01-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch04-transformation-mechanisms",
      "scene_id": "four-programs",
      "text": "A raw syntax tree can repeat the same subtree, while structural common-subexpression elimination turns that repetition into one shared result.",
      "text_sha256": "5ee19f0af86fcfe137f5d510c974b64f34d9fbe2cad26bb10493b517828e1650",
      "word_count": 20,
      "planned_start_s": 0.6,
      "planned_end_s": 10.15
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch04-transformation-mechanisms-01-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch04-transformation-mechanisms",
      "scene_id": "four-programs",
      "text": "Sharing-aware CSE-flat may also flatten safe associative structure, and CM-IR can add canonical normalization, interning, or merging.",
      "text_sha256": "b98a1de83ce79122cb421789dcbc97e8dc82402c2ef3c066589845ec0e7c05ea",
      "word_count": 17,
      "planned_start_s": 10.85,
      "planned_end_s": 20.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch04-transformation-mechanisms-02-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch04-transformation-mechanisms",
      "scene_id": "mechanism-accounting",
      "text": "A timing difference alone cannot tell us whether sharing, flattening, canonicalization, memory layout, or some other effect removed the work.",
      "text_sha256": "4ecaaec8af6e678e202609cb793f8da66715af76a2d458601519ea2ce7f031b9",
      "word_count": 20,
      "planned_start_s": 21.6,
      "planned_end_s": 31.15
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch04-transformation-mechanisms-02-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch04-transformation-mechanisms",
      "scene_id": "mechanism-accounting",
      "text": "Mechanism claims need a workload where the relevant transformation is present, plus an ablation or structural count that can distinguish competing explanations.",
      "text_sha256": "f06a8e6fa094091170744367e5684ed939776c61229fcdaccf446b87e1ae8a6b",
      "word_count": 22,
      "planned_start_s": 31.85,
      "planned_end_s": 41.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch04-transformation-mechanisms-03-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch04-transformation-mechanisms",
      "scene_id": "shared-ground",
      "text": "CM-IR should not be compared only against a weak raw tree when sharing-aware CSE-flat already captures much of the common structure.",
      "text_sha256": "d940d2bdfa44e7b7aa842de3fa87d9c15bb7e5bf647341c932a0878526fb9f54",
      "word_count": 21,
      "planned_start_s": 42.6,
      "planned_end_s": 51.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch04-transformation-mechanisms-03-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch04-transformation-mechanisms",
      "scene_id": "shared-ground",
      "text": "A fair comparison asks what additional transformation remains and whether this workload actually contains an opportunity for it to matter.",
      "text_sha256": "285eb6744c5dd1311deb4d964bdce2f347513ea5ccd1df331e810c012b440a46",
      "word_count": 20,
      "planned_start_s": 52.35,
      "planned_end_s": 61.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch05-measurement-boundaries-01-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch05-measurement-boundaries",
      "scene_id": "three-timing-boundaries",
      "text": "Preparation includes parsing, compilation, canonicalization, interning, and any data structure that must exist before evaluation begins.",
      "text_sha256": "c60e5c7774d61325b6a04fbcf2c627d937e8428debcd520508afc8d0512d2210",
      "word_count": 16,
      "planned_start_s": 0.6,
      "planned_end_s": 11.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch05-measurement-boundaries-01-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch05-measurement-boundaries",
      "scene_id": "three-timing-boundaries",
      "text": "A bare kernel times an already-built program, while a public wrapper can include setup, conversion, validation, extraction, or a complete truth-output contract.",
      "text_sha256": "7174e4092274d3005de053f23911747111c12d0ba33a34de593a1f83b8673bc8",
      "word_count": 22,
      "planned_start_s": 12.35,
      "planned_end_s": 23.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch05-measurement-boundaries-02-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch05-measurement-boundaries",
      "scene_id": "reuse-economics",
      "text": "A lower repeated-evaluation cost can be valuable only after the one-time preparation cost has been paid.",
      "text_sha256": "4428e31263bef1058ba3678c4d9e09bfbdf15f211050ed8d0e3c3efa79f20d30",
      "word_count": 16,
      "planned_start_s": 24.6,
      "planned_end_s": 35.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch05-measurement-boundaries-02-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch05-measurement-boundaries",
      "scene_id": "reuse-economics",
      "text": "The break-even point depends on how many related evaluations occur, which outputs are required, and whether the prepared representation can actually be reused unchanged.",
      "text_sha256": "a6331ef6b8853e40a6e2d22c5b898d2d171b479e4f0470c729632e813b1bff70",
      "word_count": 24,
      "planned_start_s": 36.35,
      "planned_end_s": 47.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch05-measurement-boundaries-03-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch05-measurement-boundaries",
      "scene_id": "exact-comparison-guards",
      "text": "Every comparison first needs exact output agreement, stable source identity, and a schedule that does not hand one method a systematic order advantage.",
      "text_sha256": "748f914e35acd288719457e0a0a7b12417c8ae4361652837368ee6d01b0b657b",
      "word_count": 23,
      "planned_start_s": 48.6,
      "planned_end_s": 59.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch05-measurement-boundaries-03-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch05-measurement-boundaries",
      "scene_id": "exact-comparison-guards",
      "text": "Then the interval must respect the dependence structure, and the plotted ratio must name its numerator, denominator, workload, scope, and timing boundary.",
      "text_sha256": "b309db1a52270f04b083ba030f840d39365ef827ef2e3586a034e0778ce16e54",
      "word_count": 22,
      "planned_start_s": 60.35,
      "planned_end_s": 71.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch06-corrected-evidence-01-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch06-corrected-evidence",
      "scene_id": "scoped-ratios",
      "text": "The corrected B2 and B4 result supports a workload-specific reduction for the compiled evaluator kernel, not every CM call.",
      "text_sha256": "c013ee5da4e4e8ff6498505317d9db74d8d5e1a536791f595cd4de5ca14e12ec",
      "word_count": 19,
      "planned_start_s": 0.6,
      "planned_end_s": 11.15
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch06-corrected-evidence-01-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch06-corrected-evidence",
      "scene_id": "scoped-ratios",
      "text": "EPFL AND-and-inverter workloads show parity where CSE-flat already captured the available structure, while the public wrapper remained slower on its broader boundary.",
      "text_sha256": "8b94acb34282a17b6d7957594c90279adb8092beb69435c9ffe9371b31c58f23",
      "word_count": 22,
      "planned_start_s": 11.85,
      "planned_end_s": 22.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch06-corrected-evidence-02-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch06-corrected-evidence",
      "scene_id": "three-pod-replication",
      "text": "Three guarded CPU pods reproduced an overall CM-to-CSE-flat range near zero point nine one for the same compiled-kernel workload.",
      "text_sha256": "acad267d93ec38942bf75130737ca6534c967b60581ab0ddc5ab6ca09317a820",
      "word_count": 19,
      "planned_start_s": 23.6,
      "planned_end_s": 34.15
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch06-corrected-evidence-02-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch06-corrected-evidence",
      "scene_id": "three-pod-replication",
      "text": "At live k sixteen the gap narrowed, and every pod passed exactness and source-integrity gates; replication did not convert the result into universal dominance.",
      "text_sha256": "171c2c8e8ff7ffa5afc2c3874154a06431863abe0aa4d7a65a961da70db09572",
      "word_count": 24,
      "planned_start_s": 34.85,
      "planned_end_s": 45.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch06-corrected-evidence-03-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch06-corrected-evidence",
      "scene_id": "audit-changed-headline",
      "text": "The audit did not erase the useful result; it replaced a broad headline with a stronger, reproducible statement about one workload and one boundary.",
      "text_sha256": "592f7ba3afae7a974c7d484f78e5a1183c03e470c8bb32d8f6cb6e0744a91cfb",
      "word_count": 24,
      "planned_start_s": 46.6,
      "planned_end_s": 56.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch06-corrected-evidence-03-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch06-corrected-evidence",
      "scene_id": "audit-changed-headline",
      "text": "It also retained parity and negative observations, because those results reveal where the proposed mechanism is absent or where surrounding costs dominate.",
      "text_sha256": "da2b54d13b02485d6346ac0fd6d3b2c43a63598579c4206c00c0a80189bcfb00",
      "word_count": 22,
      "planned_start_s": 57.35,
      "planned_end_s": 67.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch07-decision-rule-01-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch07-decision-rule",
      "scene_id": "choose-question-first",
      "text": "Choose the representation only after naming the required output, the reusable structure, and the pattern of repeated work.",
      "text_sha256": "311c819d911d2f6037436adb4abd96d3e78d083fa698413c78027d851a880f58",
      "word_count": 18,
      "planned_start_s": 0.6,
      "planned_end_s": 7.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch07-decision-rule-01-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch07-decision-rule",
      "scene_id": "choose-question-first",
      "text": "Ambient width alone did not yield a reliable selector, and no evidence supports choosing an engine from its label.",
      "text_sha256": "74c183b107036868391f8635d570cc6003e34af34e85ddde11f164dc2b461007",
      "word_count": 19,
      "planned_start_s": 8.35,
      "planned_end_s": 15.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch07-decision-rule-02-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch07-decision-rule",
      "scene_id": "four-part-check",
      "text": "For every performance statement, name the workload, required output, transformation, and exact timed path.",
      "text_sha256": "fff7cca52d0ac6d0a3ed6d0cdc7f6accebd0b5629be2bae09a144d81da3b8a8f",
      "word_count": 14,
      "planned_start_s": 16.6,
      "planned_end_s": 23.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch07-decision-rule-02-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch07-decision-rule",
      "scene_id": "four-part-check",
      "text": "Then verify exactness, source identity, uncertainty, and reuse assumptions before transferring the result.",
      "text_sha256": "4827ad1ee9707639b6e444533cb033961d0f51c4bd4c026fb94573258aa02ba4",
      "word_count": 13,
      "planned_start_s": 24.35,
      "planned_end_s": 31.45
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch07-decision-rule-03-1",
      "chapter_id": "ch07-decision-rule",
      "scene_id": "final-takeaway",
      "text": "An explicit CM is an exact dense truth layout, while CM-IR is a canonical reusable program representation.",
      "text_sha256": "0a4f447f0852a4840acb57f0e2ed0ea7607f2840a24e00a444f06e627dcebc05",
      "word_count": 17,
      "planned_start_s": 32.6,
      "planned_end_s": 39.65
    },
    {
      "cue_id": "ch07-decision-rule-03-2",
      "chapter_id": "ch07-decision-rule",
      "scene_id": "final-takeaway",
      "text": "Performance belongs to a workload and measured boundary; precise coordinates turn caution into action.",
      "text_sha256": "aaa48b87086585489d6d1a2ba399e12c16ba0222580011f3df8f1297a329d9cb",
      "word_count": 14,
      "planned_start_s": 40.35,
      "planned_end_s": 47.45
    }
  ],
  "status": "rendered",
  "content_hash": "a1e4f80c44de5c86b4bbfc0f98dd6fb93ad44af38c6dd89fc9a8dce3fc267857"
}
